@startuml ChatLifecycle

!include ../_style.puml

title Chat message lifecycle (send + cross-client reconcile + typing)

actor "User A" as user_a
actor "User B" as user_b

box "User A clients" #EEF2F8
participant "Tab 1\n(active chat)" as tab_a1
participant "Tab 2\n(user chats list)" as tab_a2
end box

box "User B clients" #EEF2F8
participant "Tab 3\n(active chat)" as tab_b
end box

box "Backend" #F8EFE5
participant "ChatMessagesListCreateView\n(DRF)" as view
database "Database" as db
participant "Channels layer\n(topic chat.<uuid>)" as channels
end box

note over tab_a1, tab_b
A and B subscribe to the chat topic via useChatWsEvents (-> useTopicSubscription).
Topic-group membership is reference-counted in WSClient, so the
subscription holds while ChatBox is mounted on any tab.
end note

== Subscribe ==
tab_a1 -> channels : ws action "subscribe"\n{ topic: "chat.<uuid>" }
tab_b -> channels : ws action "subscribe"\n{ topic: "chat.<uuid>" }

== Typing (throttled, 3s interval) ==
user_a -> tab_a1 : keystroke in ChatMessageForm
tab_a1 -> channels : ws action "typing"\n{ topic: "chat.<uuid>" }
note right of channels : backend caps to 1 send / 2s per group\n(TypingWSActionHandler)
channels -->> tab_b : ws event "chat.typing"\n{ user_uuid, display_name }
tab_b -> user_b : show TypingIndicator\n(TTL 5s, decays locally)

== Send message ==
user_a -> tab_a1 : submit message
tab_a1 -> view : POST /users/{A}/chats/{uuid}/messages\n{ content, attachment? }
view -> db : insert Publication (Chat scope)
view -> channels : send_ws_event(topic_group("chat", uuid),\n"chat.messages.changed", { chat_uuid })
view --> tab_a1 : 201 Created\n{ publication }
note right of tab_a1
useCreateChatMessage onSuccess
invalidates publicationKeys.chatMessages(uuid)
and publicationKeys.userChats(A)
end note
tab_a1 -> view : refetch GET /users/{A}/chats/{uuid}/messages

channels -->> tab_a1 : ws event "chat.messages.changed"
channels -->> tab_a2 : ws event "chat.messages.changed"
channels -->> tab_b : ws event "chat.messages.changed"

note over tab_a1, tab_b
useUserChatsWsEvents invalidates:
  * publicationKeys.chatMessages(chat_uuid)
  * publicationKeys.chatAttachments(chat_uuid)
  * userChats list
Each tab refetches only the queries currently mounted in it.
end note

tab_a2 -> view : refetch GET /users/{A}/chats (preview list updates)
tab_b -> view : refetch GET /users/{B}/chats/{uuid}/messages

== Scroll anchor on incoming message ==
note over tab_b
useScrollAnchor + useNewMessagesIndicator:
if the user is scrolled away from the bottom when a new message lands,
the scroll position is held in place and a NewMessagesIndicator
is shown until the user scrolls down or clicks the indicator.
end note

@enduml
